description "sudo policy hardening: own pty, own logfile, short credential cache"

supports "fedora" "rhel" "debian" "ubuntu"

mode "/etc/sudoers.d/99-hardening" "0440"

// The one claim in this collection that needs no gate. `Req-10.2.5` resolves to
// `sudo_add_use_pty` on all three datastreams -- first in document order on the
// deb pair too, ahead of the five `audit_rules_usergroup_modification_*` that
// also carry it -- and `use_pty` is what this module sets. Checked 2026-09-07
// rather than assumed, because the sibling modules show that a number naming
// one rule on Fedora routinely names another elsewhere. Only the Fedora leg
// scans, so what this buys today is that the claim would still be true if a
// deb leg ever could.
satisfies {
    pci-dss "Req-10.2.5"
}
